{"name":"Venice Square","hex":"#e6c591","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"square","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A polygon with four straight sides of equal length and four right angles; an equilateral rectangle; a regular quadrilateral.","Something characterized by a square, or nearly square, form.\nA cell in a grid."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Shaped like a square (the polygon).","Forming a right angle (90°)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/square"}],"entries":[{"title":"Venice","blocks":[{"text":"Venice is a coastal city in northeastern Italy and the capital of the region of Veneto, as well as the Metropolitan City of Venice. It is built on a group of 126 islands that are separated by expanses of open water and by canals; portions of the city are linked by 472 bridges."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Venezia_aerial_view.jpg/330px-Venezia_aerial_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venice"},{"title":"Square","blocks":[{"text":"In geometry, a square is a regular quadrilateral. It has four straight sides of equal length and four equal angles. Squares are special cases of rectangles, which have four equal angles, and of rhombuses, which have four equal sides. As with all rectangles, a square's angles are right angles, making adjacent sides perpendicular. The area of a square is the side length multiplied by itself, and so in algebra, multiplying a number by itself is called squaring."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Square_with_offset_tick_marks.svg/330px-Square_with_offset_tick_marks.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Square"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Rialto_vista_dietra-camerlenghi.JPG/500px-Rialto_vista_dietra-camerlen